---
/**
 * Book I, Ch. XIII, Prop. 1: a variational autoencoder's training path. The
 * encoder returns a distribution, the code is drawn from it, and the loss
 * has two terms: reconstruction, and the distance from the encoder's
 * distribution to the prior that generation will draw from.
 */
---
<svg class="fig" viewBox="0 0 440 330" role="img" aria-labelledby="vae-t vae-d" style="--fig-min: 0px">
  <title id="vae-t">A variational autoencoder and its two loss terms</title>
  <desc id="vae-d">
    An input x enters the encoder, which outputs a mean and a standard
    deviation. A noise sample epsilon from a standard normal enters from below,
    and the code is the mean plus the standard deviation times epsilon. The
    decoder turns the code into a distribution over x. One loss term measures
    how badly the decoder explains x; the other is the KL divergence from the
    encoder's distribution to the standard normal prior.
  </desc>

  <text x="8" y="23" class="t-lab">training path</text>

  <rect x="8" y="112" width="40" height="36" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="28" y="135" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">x</text>
  <line x1="48" y1="130" x2="64" y2="130" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="64,125 74,130 64,135" class="head" />

  <rect x="76" y="106" width="78" height="48" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="115" y="127" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">encoder</text>
  <text x="115" y="144" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">q(z | x)</text>

  <line x1="154" y1="120" x2="176" y2="104" class="wire" />
  <line x1="154" y1="140" x2="176" y2="156" class="wire" />
  <rect x="176" y="90" width="34" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="193" y="109" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">μ</text>
  <rect x="176" y="142" width="34" height="28" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="193" y="161" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">σ</text>

  <line x1="210" y1="104" x2="240" y2="124" class="wire" />
  <line x1="210" y1="156" x2="240" y2="136" class="wire" />
  <circle cx="252" cy="130" r="13" class="a3" opacity="0.22" />
  <circle cx="252" cy="130" r="13" class="s3" stroke-width="2" />
  <text x="252" y="135" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">z</text>
  <text x="252" y="96" class="t-key" text-anchor="middle">z = μ + σ ε</text>

  <circle cx="252" cy="214" r="16" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="252" y="219" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">ε</text>
  <text x="276" y="219" class="t-sm">~ N(0, 1)</text>
  <line x1="252" y1="198" x2="252" y2="155" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="247,155 252,145 257,155" class="head" />

  <line x1="265" y1="130" x2="282" y2="130" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="282,125 292,130 282,135" class="head" />
  <rect x="294" y="106" width="78" height="48" class="bx-fill" />
  <text x="333" y="127" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">decoder</text>
  <text x="333" y="144" class="t-sm" text-anchor="middle">p(x | z)</text>
  <line x1="372" y1="130" x2="390" y2="130" class="wire" />
  <polygon points="390,125 400,130 390,135" class="head" />
  <text x="404" y="135" class="t-md">x̂</text>

  <path d="M 193 90 V 66 H 214" class="dash" />
  <text x="218" y="70" class="t-key">KL( q(z | x) ‖ N(0, 1) )</text>

  <path d="M 412 150 V 262 H 28 V 158" class="dash" />
  <polygon points="23,160 28,148 33,160" class="head" />
  <text x="220" y="280" class="t-md" text-anchor="middle">reconstruction: −log p(x | z)</text>

  <text x="8" y="304" class="t-sm">Training draws z from the encoder's distribution.</text>
  <text x="8" y="323" class="t-sm">Generating draws it from N(0, 1). The KL keeps them close.</text>
</svg>
